{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "base_revision": "6dc7b6c94fa5fa22b03eb9586d9b9390e83226e1",
  "decision": "pre_release_break",
  "rationale": "First application-facing alea facade with feature-aware modules and prelude. Existing implementation APIs remain inventoried. External consumers and generated code now use alea alone; no compatibility aliases are retained for the unpublished direct-crate interface. New facade feature surfaces have no earlier published baseline. Sampling exports are now explicitly enumerated rather than glob-imported; all previously exported sampling paths are retained. The snapshot renderer records the individual aliases instead of a glob marker. Remove unused public positive_finite, finite_or_neg_inf and log_accept_ratio helpers that silently coerce invalid numerical values. No compatibility aliases or replacement coercions are introduced; checked target boundaries and production acceptance code are unchanged. Add explicit bounded Wiener4/5/7 joint time and boundary sampling methods, without changing default inference or promoting their finite validation scope. Add optional componentwise Wiener4/5 real-arithmetic truncation reports; floating-point roundoff is explicitly excluded and the existing fast path is unchanged.",
